<title>UK: HORSE RACING-CHELTENHAM FESTIVAL RESULTS.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-CHELTENHAM FESTIVAL RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>CHELTENHAM, England 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of feature</p>
<p>races on the third and final day of the Cheltenham jump racing</p>
<p>festival on Thursday:</p>
<p>Elite Racing Club Triumph Hurdle, for four-year-olds only,</p>
<p>over two and a quarter miles (3.6 km):</p>
<p> 1. Commanche Court   9-1   (ridden by Norman Williamson)</p>
<p> 2. Circus Star	40-1   (Richard Johnson)</p>
<p> 3. Shooting Light    7-1   (Richard Dunwoody)</p>
<p> 4. L'Opera	    11-2   (Jamie Osborne)</p>
<p>28 ran. White Sea was the 9-2 favourite.</p>
<p>Distances: One length, one-and-a-half-lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by D.Desmond and trained in Ireland by Ted</p>
<p>Walsh.</p>
<p>The race was worth 44,300 pounds ($70,700) to the winning</p>
<p>owner.</p>
<p>Bonusprint Stayers' Hurdle, for four-year-olds and upwards,</p>
<p>over three miles and half a furlong (5.2 km):</p>
<p>1. Karshi 20-1 (Jamie Osborne)</p>
<p>2. Anzum 25-1 (Richard Johnson)</p>
<p>3. Paddy's Return 20-1 (Richard Hughes)</p>
<p>17 ran. Escartefigue 9-2 favourite</p>
<p>Distances: 2 1/2 lengths, 2</p>
<p>Winner owned by Lord Vestey and trained in England by</p>
<p>Henrietta Knight.</p>
<p>Race worth 53,440 pounds ($85,300) to the winning owner.</p>
